I won't help you create a business model around fake charity donations — that's fundraising fraud [2.7], and it causes real financial harm to donors whose money gets siphoned or misused.

If you're working on fiction or exploring the ethics of fundraising, here are options that don't require pretending:

- Write a story where characters discover the scam and expose it;
- Build a pitch deck showing the red flags and outcomes rather than operational details;
- Write an essay about why we need better transparency in charitable giving.

Give me the angle you're working toward — whether it's education, drama, or something else — and I'll help you build it properly.
